And I do have like an incantation.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.320
I say something right
before I go on stage.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.460
I wanna share it with you guys.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:33.840
- I know that's your own to have,

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.310
but is it like a superstitious thing?

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:36.570
Because I have something similar.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:37.710
- It's not so much superstitious,

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:38.760
it's more of just like something

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.770
where I demand something for myself.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.050
I'm not like, "I hope
it goes well tonight."

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:44.040
It's like a (thumps chest).

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:46.110
This is something like
I'm going out there,

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:47.400
I'm gonna serve this audience.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:50.070
I'm gonna give them
everything I absolutely have.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:50.903
Every night.

00:08:50.903 --> 00:08:51.736
So there's no question

00:08:51.736 --> 00:08:53.190
that I'm gonna put on
the best show possible

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:54.023
every single night.

00:08:54.023 --> 00:08:55.350
There's no question.
- I love how different we are.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.370
We're gonna have to bleep this

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.637
but I literally just say to my band,

00:08:57.637 --> 00:08:58.987
"Hope we don't (bleep) up."

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:02.913
That's literally what I say.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:06.570
Hayley, have you ever given him advice

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:07.980
like doing shows and
putting shows together?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.900
'Cause it's kind of interesting, like,

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:11.820
I guess it would be like me
being with a musician, right?

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.460
You have input, like you
know what you're both doing

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:16.260
and you're both passionate and creative.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.210
Do you ever like, brainstorm together?

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:19.320
- Yeah, definitely.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:22.500
I would say I'm more of a
soundboard for him though

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.690
because he has so many thoughts

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:25.740
that are going through his head.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:26.573
Oh, my gosh.

00:09:26.573 --> 00:09:28.320
He's the biggest visionary ever.

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:30.840
And I feel like I'm very grounding,

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.850
so I like organize all of his thoughts,

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.560
so I'm more logistical.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.450
Whereas he's creative

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:37.283
- Hey babe, what about this?

00:09:37.283 --> 00:09:38.116
And then we're over here.

00:09:38.116 --> 00:09:39.330
What about that?
- And I'm like, hold on.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.680
Okay, how does that even work?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:42.780
Let's bring this down.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:43.650
- You found a partner.

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:44.483
That's amazing.

00:09:44.483 --> 00:09:45.600
- We make a good team.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.433
We really do.

00:09:46.433 --> 00:09:47.266
- That's incredible.

00:09:47.266 --> 00:09:48.540
And you can be honest with each other too.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:49.373
That's the best part.

00:09:49.373 --> 00:09:50.234
When you're in a relationship,

00:09:50.234 --> 00:09:51.150
you'll be like, that looks stupid.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.402
Don't do that.

00:09:52.402 --> 00:09:53.235
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:53.235 --> 00:09:54.210
That's a real friend.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:56.160
You have a booger, like, you know.

